iven by King Louis IX of France at Péronne in September 1256 to end the War of the Flemish Succession.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/diu"><span class="enc-name">Diu</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Diu is a town and island off the southern coast of the Saurashtra peninsula in Gujarat, India.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/diuma"><span class="enc-name">Diuma</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Diuma was an Irish priest, one of four sent from Northumbria with Peada in 653 to preach to the Middle Angles.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/divan"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/divan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Divan</span><span class="enc-type">Institution</span><span class="enc-snip">The Divan was the imperial council of the Ottoman Empire, chaired by the grand vizier.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/divashtich"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/divashtich.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Divashtich</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Divashtich was the ruler of Panjikent in Sogdiana who in the early 720s claimed the titles king of Sogdiana and lord of Samarkand.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/dives-sur-mer"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/dives-sur-mer.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Dives-sur-Mer</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Dives-sur-Mer is a small town in the Calvados department of Normandy, at the mouth of the Dives.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/diviciacus-aedui"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/diviciacus-aedui.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56